      "notes": "declared equivalent: Mutates the initial value in `indegree = {n: 0 for n in nodes}` from 0 to 1 (graphkit/topo.py:26:19, change_constant_increment). This dict comprehension's keys are exactly `nodes`, and every single key in `nodes` is unconditionally overwritten immediately afterward by `for node, deps in deps_of.items(): indegree[node] = len(deps)` -- deps_of is itself built as `{n: set(...) for n in nodes}`, so deps_of.items() iterates precisely the same key set as nodes/indegree. No node's indegree value is ever read between the comprehension and that overwrite loop. Therefore the initial placeholder value (0 vs 1) is provably never observed for any input graph -- this is a true equivalent mutant, not a surviving behavioral gap, and cannot be turned into a failing hidden-test case because no input distinguishes the two versions."
    },
